Let \(0<\epsilon<1/2\) and let \(P\in\mathcal P_{d,\epsilon,M,\sigma}\) as in \cref{obj:def:model-class}.  For a block of \(m\) independent observations with joint law \(Q_P^{(m)}\), write \(V_i=Y_i/M\) and, for a cell \(k\), an arm \(a\), and an order \(j\), let
\[
U_{k,a,j}
:=
\frac{1}{(m)_{j+2}}
\sum_{i_0,\ldots,i_{j+1}\ {\rm distinct}}
V_{i_0}\mathbf 1\{X_{i_0}=k,A_{i_0}=a\}
\mathbf 1\{X_{i_1}=k\}
\prod_{t=2}^{j+1}\mathbf 1\{X_{i_t}=k,A_{i_t}=a\}
\]
be the ordered distinct-index one-mark factorial statistic.  If \(j+2\le K\), \(r+2\le K\), and \(4(K+2)^2\le m\), then for all arms \(a,b\in\{0,1\}\) the same-cell centered cross moment obeys
\[
\left|\operatorname{Cov}_{Q_P^{(m)}}\!\left(U_{k,a,j},U_{k,b,r}\right)\right|
\le
\frac{2(K+2)^2}{m}\,p_k^{j+2}p_k^{r+2}
+
e\left(\frac54p_k\right)^{r+2}
\left(\frac54p_k+\frac{r+2}{m}\right)^{j+2},
\]
where \(e=\exp(1)\).  No boundedness of \(Y\) is required.

